 # Working notes: 7a8926bd9d9f
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## Current repair
+
+Version 2.1.0 fixes the retained source-bound audit without changing canonical
+Racket authority or rule hash `e6d9cb6ee6d8`. The prior generator drew the key
+`rectangles` while advertising `n_rects`, never consumed palette controls, and
+accepted unknown/coercive overrides. It also treated two same-color cells in a
+single row as valid even though protected Racket leaves that fixture unchanged.
+
+The repaired API exposes only observable controls: `grid_h` and `grid_w` in
+4..16, `n_rects` in 1..8, and four palette families. Helpful `texture` values
+are exact palette aliases; conflicting aliases fail visibly. Rectangle count is
+constructive rather than retry-based: the grid is partitioned into disjoint
+cells at least 2x2, so every accepted count is placed or an incompatible small
+grid/count request raises a capacity error. Colors remain distinct.
+
+`self_check` now validates rectangular exact-integer grids, two occurrences per
+active color, a row and column difference for every pair, and pairwise-disjoint
+bounding rectangles. The old `no_pairs`, `single_endpoint`, and `axis_aligned`
+textures remain available only as explicit negative fixtures and are all
+rejected by the validator.
+
+Focused tests cover every count 1..8, exact dimensions, palette aliases,
+invalid controls, canonical pairs, overlap rejection, repeatability, and fresh
+mutable outputs. `workspace/repair_audit.py` is a reusable source-bound audit;
+its retained run executes 17 labels through protected Racket (all counts, all
+palettes, min/max controls, and all canonical pairs) and checks all three
+negative fixtures. No canonical source or Racket program changed. Arbitrary
+out-of-domain grids and distribution quality remain outside this finite check.
 
